  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105586",
      "title": "Configuring the TypeScript Compiler",
      "lectureOrder": 761,
      "videoOrder": 701,
      "sourceHash": "272788dd2484d8e5a24e0deef8e135c94c063d6520b672ed4260f605ffdf02f6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "Now to really conclude",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 6.53,
          "en": "this TypeScript introduction section now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.53,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "let's talk about configuring the TypeScript compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "You might recall that before when I executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 16.87,
          "en": "just npx typescript, I got this error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.87,
          "end": 20.67,
          "en": "that basically a TypeScript configuration file is missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.67,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "and that's why I had to target a specific TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 27.97,
          "en": "like this to then compile just this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.97,
          "end": 31.08,
          "en": "Now, sometimes you want to compile all the TypeScript files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.08,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "in your project in one go, and you also might want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.58,
          "en": "to configure how the TypeScript compiler behaves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 40.33,
          "en": "And for this, you can add a TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.33,
          "end": 42.2,
          "en": "compiler config file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.2,
          "end": 47.2,
          "en": "You can do this with npx tsc -- init.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.22,
          "end": 51.88,
          "en": "What this does is it adds a tsconfig.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.88,
          "end": 54.96,
          "en": "though I will say, once we work with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.96,
          "end": 58.51,
          "en": "we don't need to do that because the Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.51,
          "end": 61.617,
          "en": "get TypeScript configuration files out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.617,
          "end": 64.19,
          "en": "and you should really only change them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.19,
          "end": 66.23,
          "en": "if you know what you're doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.23,
          "end": 69.1,
          "en": "But here we now got such a TypeScript compiler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.1,
          "end": 71.14,
          "en": "configuration file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.14,
          "end": 74.3,
          "en": "And in there, we got lots of options, which we can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.3,
          "end": 76.34,
          "en": "Now, one of the most important options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.34,
          "end": 78.94,
          "en": "is the strict mode option here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.94,
          "end": 81.033,
          "en": "which by default is set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 84.55,
          "en": "When using strict mode, TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.55,
          "end": 88.16,
          "en": "as the name implies does very strict type checking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.16,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "And there are many things which it doesn't allow it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 93.78999999999999,
          "en": "like for example, values where it's not able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.3,
          "en": "to infer the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.3,
          "end": 99.47,
          "en": "You then have to explicitly set a type for those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.47,
          "end": 101.37299999999999,
          "en": "But that's just one example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.41,
          "end": 105.33,
          "en": "Now, in general, you can read through this config file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.33,
          "end": 107.33,
          "en": "to understand these different settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.33,
          "end": 109.34,
          "en": "And of course, I do talk about them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.34,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "in way greater detail in my full TypeScript course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.67,
          "en": "As I said, with Angular projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.67,
          "end": 118.7,
          "en": "we get a TypeScript file out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.7,
          "end": 121.57,
          "en": "and therefore, this is not really the focus here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.57,
          "end": 125.5,
          "en": "because this default Angular TypeScript compiler file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.5,
          "end": 127.21,
          "en": "will do the trick for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.21,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "and we don't really need to change them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 131.71,
          "en": "Nonetheless, this is how you can configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.71,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "the TypeScript compiler and feel free to dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "into these different options to play around with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 140.47,
          "en": "But with that, we now got all those important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.47,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "basics out of the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "And now with that, you're definitely ready to dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 147.163,
          "en": "into Angular and TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
